## Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:**
- Make ChatView responsive for mobile devices (< 768px breakpoints)
- Implement mobile-first layout strategy for sidebar navigation
- Optimize header and input areas for touch interaction
- Ensure proper spacing, sizing for mobile viewing
- Maintain full functionality while adapting visual presentation

**Strategic Approach:**
1. Add responsive classes to ChatView main layout (flex-col on mobile)
2. Implement mobile drawer/sheet for sidebar (toggle-able)
3. Update ChatSidebar for mobile responsiveness (full-width sheet on small screens)
4. Optimize modal sizing for mobile devices
5. Adjust spacing and typography for touch-friendly interface
6. Ensure proper viewport stacking for mobile interaction

**Dependencies & Risks:**
- ChatView references multiple child components (Chat, ChatSidebar, ChatViewHeader)
- Need to preserve existing desktop layout while adding mobile alternatives
- Touch interactions require larger tap targets (44px minimum)
- Modal modals need proper viewport sizing on small screens
- Sidebar drawer behavior must integrate seamlessly with existing state management

